<title>USA: Ciatti's Q1 hurt by full-service units.</title>
<headline>Ciatti's Q1 hurt by full-service units.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ciatti's Inc, which reported a loss for the September 29 first quarter, said its loss from operations primarily reflected declining sales at the company's full-service restaurants.</p>
<p>It also cited operating losses related to the company's four new Bruegger's Bagel Bakery outlets.</p>
<p>The company posted a first-quarter loss of $0.70 per share, compared with a loss of $0.25 per share in the corresponding period of 1995. Sales fell to $4.27 million from $4.21 million.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
